**New Evidence**
I kept a compact set of distinct 2022 URLs that cover basic services, social protection, education, crisis handling, and end-of-year household conditions.

- UNICEF country dashboard shows very high basic water and sanitation access, plus basic dignity indicators.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Child-Related SDG Progress Assessment for China","publisher":"UNICEF DATA","publication_date":"best available: current dashboard with 2022 indicators","url":"https://data.unicef.org/sdgs/country/chn/","claim":"For 2022, China’s UNICEF dashboard shows 98% basic drinking-water access, 96% basic sanitation access, 97% basic handwashing access, and 0% open defecation.","locator":"environment indicators on the China country dashboard","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"UN agency data dashboard is strong for country-level service-access context, though it is a dashboard summary rather than a ruler-specific evaluation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 country indicators shown on the dashboard.","ruler_attribution":"Country-level baseline evidence only; it is not direct proof of Xi’s personal management, but it is relevant welfare context under his rule.","contrary_evidence":["This is a national dashboard, not ruler-specific attribution.","The dashboard does not by itself show service quality or political prioritization."],"lenses":["6B.2","6B.8","6B.10"]}

