SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Li Xi gets graft-busting role on China's new Standing Committee","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/10/24/china-congress-li","claim":"Reuters said Li Xi was placed in charge of the party's powerful graft-busting body and that anti-corruption had become a signature tool of Xi's rule, helping consolidate power by replacing rivals with loyalists.","locator":"lead paragraphs and Reuters analysis section","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong contemporaneous Reuters reporting with direct relevance to anti-corruption governance and elite control.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"October 2022 congress aftermath.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Xi's governing style because it describes how he uses the discipline apparatus and whom he trusted to lead it.","contrary_evidence":["The CCDI can also function as a genuine anti-graft institution.","The article does not identify a specific personal financial conflict for Xi himself."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China to increase scrutiny of statistical data to curb fraud","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-18","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/china-to-increase-scrutiny-of-statistical-data-to-curb-fraud-2787208","claim":"Reuters reported that the CCDI said statistical data fraud remained prominent, that some local authorities had issued secret instructions to manipulate data, and that the party would intensify scrutiny and accountability.","locator":"opening paragraphs and CCDI quotation","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting with concrete anti-fraud claims and clear period fit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022 enforcement posture.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Xi-era governance because the CCDI and party accountability system operated under his leadership, though the local falsification itself was done by subnational officials.","contrary_evidence":["This is evidence of enforcement against falsification, not proof Xi personally told the truth in a given case.","It also shows that data distortion remained a live problem."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China punishes local officials for falsifying economic data","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://m.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/china-punishes-local-officials-for-falsifying-economic-data-2830947?ampMode=1","claim":"Reuters reported that the National Bureau of Statistics said multiple local officials were demoted or dismissed for falsifying data, including 45 officials in Xingtai, 38 in Henan, and 22 in Guizhou.","locator":"opening paragraphs and province-by-province figures","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Strong Reuters reporting on a dated enforcement action with specific sanction counts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects the Xi-era discipline environment and anti-fraud posture rather than Xi personally issuing each sanction.","contrary_evidence":["It remains a local-enforcement story, not a direct Xi statement or personal correction.","Punishment of subordinates does not itself prove Xi’s own candor."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China tightens regulation of business activities of officials' relatives","publisher":"english.www.gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-06-19","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/policies/latestreleases/202206/19/content_WS62b15beec6d02e533532c747.html","claim":"The CPC Central Committee issued rules requiring officials to report relatives' business activities annually, imposing stricter prohibitions on higher-level officials, and warning that false reporting would be punished severely.","locator":"main body of the article","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary policy text with explicit reporting and prohibition requirements, though it is still official self-description.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022 policy action.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Xi-era party governance and its integrity controls; it does not prove Xi's own family conduct, but it directly addresses family conflict-of-interest rules under his rule.","contrary_evidence":["A rule against family business is not proof that family self-dealing was absent.","The article is official and does not independently verify compliance."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China further reins in business activities of officials' families","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-20","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/06/20/china-corruption","claim":"Reuters reported that senior officials' spouses and children would have to withdraw from business activities or officials could face job adjustments, and it noted that many corruption cases involved family members as intermediaries for abusing influence.","locator":"lead paragraphs and Reuters analysis section","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting adds independent context and explains the anti-nepotism rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022 policy implementation and context.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Xi-era governance because it describes a Central Committee rule issued under his leadership, though not a personal finding against Xi himself.","contrary_evidence":["This is preventive regulation, not proof of Xi-family profiteering in 2022.","It may reflect a genuine attempt to reduce conflicts rather than conceal them."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Xi screens for loyalty ahead of party congress","publisher":"Intelligence Online","publication_date":"2022-10-10","url":"https://www.intelligenceonline.com/asia-pacific/2022/10/10/xi-screens-for-loyalty-ahead-of-party-congress%2C109832839-art","claim":"Intelligence Online reported that the CCP approved a new regulation to assess political loyalty across civil servants, military command, and state-company directors within weeks, with the goal of removing disloyalty quickly.","locator":"article summary paragraph","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized reporting with a concrete contemporaneous claim, though the article is subscriber-gated and the claim is captured in the summary snippet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022 pre-congress rule-setting.","ruler_attribution":"Directly linked to Xi because the loyalty test was framed around his political project and the coming congress.","contrary_evidence":["The article is about political loyalty screening, not financial self-dealing.","It is an indirect sign of control, not a direct integrity finding."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.7","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Xi Jinping's new politburo emerges from lengthy and secret selection procedure","publisher":"Intelligence Online","publication_date":"2022-11-21","url":"https://www.intelligenceonline.com/asia-pacific/2022/11/21/xi-jinping-s-new-politburo-emerges-from-lengthy-and-secret-selection-procedure%2C109866240-eve","claim":"Intelligence Online reported that all new Politburo and discipline-inspection appointees were subjected to unprecedented scrutiny by Xi's closest collaborators, and that some factions saw their influence wiped out.","locator":"opening summary paragraph","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist reporting on elite selection and secrecy; the summary snippet provides the key factual claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-period 2022 post-congress selection.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Xi's control over personnel selection and the narrow circle around him that performed the scrutiny.","contrary_evidence":["The source shows scrutiny, but not independent scrutiny of Xi by outside institutions.","It is more about intra-elite vetting than public honesty."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.7","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Xi Jinping brings Beijing's second-most influential body to heel before CCP Congress","publisher":"Intelligence Online","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.intelligenceonline.com/asia-pacific/2022/05/27/xi-jinping-brings-beijing-s-second-most-influential-body-to-heel-before-ccp-congress%2C109787840-art","claim":"Intelligence Online reported that the Communist Youth League was being restructured because it had gotten in the way of Xi Jinping's political ambitions.","locator":"opening summary paragraph","source_type":"other","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialist reporting with a direct claim on factional restructuring under Xi; the snippet is sufficient for the factual claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Xi because it describes a political reorganization driven by his ambitions and the neutralization of a rival base.","contrary_evidence":["This is about factional power, not a direct financial conflict.","It still does not prove personal enrichment."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Leaked Records Reveal Offshore Holdings of China’s Elite","publisher":"ICIJ","publication_date":"2014-01-21","url":"https://www.icij.org/investigations/offshore/leaked-records-reveal-offshore-holdings-of-chinas-elite/","claim":"ICIJ reported that Xi Jinping’s brother-in-law Deng Jiagui held a secretive offshore company and that Xi had crushed a grassroots movement calling for officials to publicly declare their assets.","locator":"the 'Princelings go offshore' section","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Major cross-border investigative project based on leaked records; old but concrete and well-documented.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Historical context relevant to Xi’s tenure; not specific to 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but important: it concerns Xi’s close family and his wider political environment, not a formal Xi declaration in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["The offshore company records predate 2022 and do not prove 2022 conduct.","The evidence concerns a relative and the broader elite, not Xi's own personal accounts."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.7"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 distinct documents across Reuters syndications, Bloomberg analyses, Intelligence Online, official CPC/State Council materials, and ICIJ investigations.

Kept evidence covered these themes:
- Xi’s 2022 congress consolidation and loyalist staffing.
- Secretive, loyalty-based selection and vetting.
- Anti-corruption as a political tool and the graft-busting apparatus.
- Anti-data-fraud enforcement and corrections.
- Rules restricting officials’ relatives and family business activity.
- Historical offshore-wealth context tied to Xi’s brother-in-law.

Rejected or de-prioritized:
- Duplicate Reuters syndications of the same congress story.
- Broad authoritarianism or censorship pieces that did not add a direct personal-integrity nexus beyond the already used appointment/scrutiny evidence.
- 2023-2026 follow-ups that were useful only as retrospective color, not target-period 2022 evidence.
- Generic China corruption indicators and country-level governance scores, which are context only and not personal-conduct evidence.
- Articles that repeated the same family-business or anti-corruption rule without adding a materially distinct claim.

**Remaining Gaps**
- No direct 2022 public filing or independent audit of Xi’s own assets surfaced.
- No clear 2022 evidence of Xi personally admitting error or making a costly factual correction in public.
- The strongest negative evidence is indirect: loyalist appointments, secrecy, and control of scrutiny rather than a single documented self-enrichment case in 2022.
- The strongest positive evidence is also indirect: anti-data-fraud enforcement and family-business restrictions, which show some attempt to constrain abuse but do not prove Xi’s own personal separation from interests.
- More search would help if you want a sharper answer on personal assets, family wealth, or independent findings about Xi’s immediate circle, but I did not find a clean 2022 documentary trail for that within the time-bounded evidence.

