SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China to expedite delivery of policy package to keep economy stable","publisher":"english.www.gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-06-02","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/premier/news/202206/02/content_WS6297eddec6d02e533532b9c5.html","claim":"China would speed up implementation of a package of policy measures to maintain stable economic performance, and the package was intended to improve the speed and effectiveness of policy implementation and ensure eligible firms and households benefited.","locator":"lines 45-52","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government implementation notice with concrete administrative instructions and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate-to-strong attribution: the package was tied to the central policy orientation from the Central Economic Work Conference and Government Work Report, within Xi’s governing system.","contrary_evidence":["The notice describes implementation intentions; it does not by itself verify local compliance or results."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.8"]}
- 2022-06-09 follow-through: State Council task forces inspected 12 provinces and reported bottlenecks, then ordered barrier removal and better policy effects.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"China to remove bottlenecks in policy implementation to produce greater effects for keeping economic activity stable","publisher":"english.www.gov.cn / Xinhua","publication_date":"2022-06-09","url":"https://english.www.gov.cn/premier/news/202206/09/content_WS62a1285ec6d02e533532be0c.html","claim":"After special inspections in 12 provinces, the State Council said it would remove barriers, improve support measures, and better bring out policy effects for steady growth, market entities, employment, foreign trade, and investment.","locator":"lines 45-50","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official record of inspection and corrective follow-up, not just announcement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate attribution through the State Council and central economic policy chain under Xi’s leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The existence of inspections implies implementation problems remained significant."],"lenses":["8B.5","8B.6","8B.8"]}
- 2022-04-15 monetary easing: PBC cut bank reserve requirements to support the real economy and market entities.
